MGAVIDEO palette-fade FUN_0000_04f1 (post-intro, e446 -> c594=04cd -> 04d8 -> 04f1): reconstruct the
CF==0 fade path that Ghidra folded to `do{}while(true)` -> the post-intro HANG.

After the first intro (TITLE.KDV) ends, engine FUN_0000_e446 does `(*c594)(); e584(0x4404); (*c59c)()`.
The c594 method resolves to driver FUN_0000_04cd -> 04d8 -> 04f1, a palette-fade set-up.  Ghidra
mis-modelled 04f1 (asm image 0x4f1..0x5b6):
  - the `call [DGROUP:0xe4]` (device-object method c0e4, args ax=0x300/bx=0x788/cx=ds) had its args
    AND its CF-out dropped; the CF (`jb 0x587`) selects INSTANT (CF=1) vs FADE (CF=0).
  - Ghidra invented the branch condition `bVar6 = param_2 < param_4` (false here: 0xff < 0) and
    rendered the entire CF==0 fade body (tick-wait + DAC save + install continuation) as an infinite
    `do{}while(true)` -> the engine hangs the moment it starts the post-intro fade.
  - the INSTANT path's palette clear lost its ES=[c782] base (di used as a bare host pointer).
Reconstructed faithfully from asm:
  0x4f1 [c786]=0; [c5e8]=0; [0632]=0; [0634]=0x10000/param_1; [0638]=(param_2-param_4)+1;
        [0636]=param_4; [063a]=param_3
  0x52d call [DGROUP:0xe4](ax=0x300,bx=0x788,cx=ds) ; 0x531 jb 0x587 (CF -> instant)
  FADE (0x533): wait one INT-8 tick [DGROUP:0x44e] ; inc [0x738] ; [0636]*=3 ; [0638]*=3 ;
        out 0x3c7,0 ; read 0x300 DAC bytes -> es:[c788] ; dec [0x738] ; [c5e8]=0x5b8 (FUN_05b8) ; retf
  INSTANT (0x587): es=[c782] ; di=[0636]*3 ; clear [0638]*3 bytes ; [c780]=0x782 ; [c786]=1 ; retf
DGROUP:0xe4 is an as-yet uninstalled device-object method vector (== 0 at runtime, same gap class as
patch 049's 0xcc/0xd0) so the call traps (no-op) and CF stays 0 -> the FADE path (the intended
high-detail title behaviour).  Threaded via the shim CF global g_fist_cf so the real method's CF takes
over once 0xe4 is installed.  The tick-wait is cooperatively pumped (patch 017/072/3a14 class); the
fade then advances over subsequent vblanks via the c5e8 continuation dispatched by the retrace ISR.
